Inspiration
-----------

Assmosis started from the shape of NextMeeting's public ACA list:

  https://nextmeeting.org/0BF67B1D-444F-45F5-BA5B-E3ADD7E4C30B.html

That page was the reference for the product: a weekly meeting list, times
shown in the viewer's zone, add a meeting, send feedback, and a printable
week. "Template" overstates it. It was not a code template. No HTML, script,
or stylesheet from that page, and no source from the NextMeeting project, is
included here.

The "Code on Github" link on that page points at DanielGuru/nextmeeting,
which does not exist. The public project is:

  https://github.com/NextMeeting/next-meeting-static-site

That repository (gulp, Alpine.js, Tailwind) has no LICENSE file. Its code
stays with its authors under whatever terms they set. Assmosis is not a fork
of it. Alpine.js is not a dependency. A search of this tree does not contain
that project's source.

Names that still say nextmeeting
---------------------------------

A few identifiers were left in place so existing data on a device would keep
loading. They are labels, not copied code:

  src/lib/meetings/store.ts     localStorage "nextmeeting-aca-v1", "nextmeeting-theme"
  src/lib/meetings/typeface.ts  localStorage "nextmeeting-type"
  src/lib/meetings/idb.ts       IndexedDB database name "nextmeeting"
  src/components/import-export.tsx
                                downloaded filenames "nextmeeting-template"
  src/components/session-details.tsx
                                calendar UID host "@nextmeeting"
                                calendar PRODID "-//TheRooms//EN"

The menu used to include Send Feedback, aimed at feedback@nextmeeting.app.
That is NextMeeting's address. The item has been removed.

Menu labels such as "Add a Meeting" and "Printable Weekly List" follow the
same jobs as that ACA page. The wording is ordinary, not a copied program.

